cumbersome and provides only an example when $x=-{Q_H}/6$,
$y={Q_\Phi}/2$). 
One may check that for this choice of charges the resulting coefficients
$\bc{1,2}$ in the interaction terms~(\ref{eq:48}) are non-zero, which leads to
interesting phenomenology to be discussed in the next section.

